### Broken Item State
When a piece of equipment's vanilla durability reaches zero:
- `broken` is set to true
- The item does not disappear — it remains in the player's inventory
- All enchantment effects are suppressed
- All Tool effectivity is suppressed, tools, weapon and armor provide no use while broken
- XP accrual is halted
- The item name gains a red `[BROKEN]` prefix
- The item renderer applies a strong red tint to the item sprite via Mixin, making it visually distinct at a glance
- Tooltip shows "Broken — repair at an Anvil"
- Repairing at an Anvil with the appropriate material removes the `broken` flag, restores the normal amount of durability, and resumes normal function. Repair cost scales with item level (see Anvil Changes).

---

### Glint System
Mixin into `ItemStack.hasGlint()`:
- Always returns `false` for any item with our custom component, unless `readyToLevelUp` is true
- Items are always visually mundane until the level-up moment, regardless of internally slotted enchantments
- Glint disappears again immediately upon leveling up

