### Loot Integration
A global loot modifier runs post-generation on all loot tables (vanilla and modded). For every generated equipment item that already has vanilla enchantments:
- Those enchantments are converted into 1–2 bonus slots (`bonusSlots`) in the component
- The vanilla enchantment tags are stripped
- These slots appear beneath the standard slots in the tooltip, prefixed with ★ in gold text
- They are upgradeable through the enchanting table normally
- The item still has its full 4 standard slots available to earn through play

Found enchanted loot is therefore always meaningfully ahead of freshly crafted gear.

---

### Enchantment Books: Fully Disabled
- Global loot modifier strips enchanted books from all loot table outputs (catches modded tables automatically)
- Mixin blocks villager enchanted book trades
- Mixin blocks fishing from producing enchanted books
- Custom enchanting table never produces books
- Net result: enchanted books are unobtainable by any means in the game

---

### Anvil Changes
- Combining two equipment items is blocked (Mixin returns empty result)
- Repairing with materials still works
- Vanilla "too expensive" scaling (prior work penalty) is removed
- Repair cost instead scales with item level — configurable base cost + flat increase per level
- Repairing a `broken` item with materials removes the broken state and restores partial durability as normal

---

### Grindstone Changes
- Mixin strips all custom slot and level data (standard and bonus slots) from the item
- Returns player XP equivalent to the combined vanilla XP value of all slotted enchantments
- Does not affect durability
- Behaves exactly as players would expect from the vanilla grindstone, extended to the new system

---

### Death Behavior
- Config toggle: **"Keep Leveled Equipment on Death"** (default: off)
- When enabled, acts as keep-inventory specifically for any item with our custom component — armor, tools, weapons with any level data are kept on death
- Non-equipment items still drop normally
- Does not interact with or require the global `keepInventory` gamerule

---

### Config (Mod Menu, hand-rolled screen)
- `baseXP` per item category (Sword, Axe, Pickaxe, Shovel, Hoe, Helmet, Chestplate, Leggings, Boots, Fishing Rod, and a default fallback)
- XP scaling multiplier (default 1.2, global)
- XP display threshold (minimum gain to show floating number)
- Durability restore % on level up (default 25%)
- Reroll costs per slot count (5 / 10 / 15 / 20 / 25)
- Legendary upgrade probability
- Material tier upgrade ladder (ordered list — default Wood → Stone → Iron → Diamond → Netherite, gold excluded, editable)
- Enchantment offer weights (upgrade vs new slot probability)
- Anvil repair base cost and per-level cost increase
- Keep Leveled Equipment on Death toggle (default off)
- Broken item mechanic toggle (default on)

